course: dictionary
lesson: 9686
title: Enough: the word suffice
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: Suffice is a formal word that means to be enough. When something suffices, you need nothing more. In everyday talk people would say «that will do» or «that's enough», so suffice is a word you will meet in exams, official letters and maths.
explain: Use context to check. «£5 will suffice» is a maths sentence about money. Swap in the meaning: «£5 will be enough» still makes sense, so suffice means be enough.
explain: Suffice can start a phrase too. «Suffice it to say» means «I will only say this, because it is enough». The writer is telling you that this one point is enough, so they will stop there.
explain: Look at this sentence: «The Rat was a self-sufficing sort of animal, rooted to the land». Self-sufficing has suffice inside it, a hint that the Rat could manage on his own. You can see the same root word in both.
fact: Suffice is a verb. Its forms are suffices, sufficed and sufficing.
fact: Suffice means to be enough.
fact: «Suffice it to say» means «I will only say this, because it is enough».
fact: «£5 will suffice» means £5 is enough money.
fact: Suffice is a formal word. In everyday talk, people say «that will do» or «that's enough».
exercise: Maths homework says «£5 will suffice for the bus fare». What does suffice mean? | *Be enough | Be too much | Be spent on sweets | Be lost
exercise: Which phrase means «I will only say this, because it is enough»? | Sue for peace | *Suffice it to say | Surface at once | Suffer in silence
exercise: «The Rat was a self-sufficing sort of animal.» Find and copy the word that has suffice inside it. | animal | sort | rooted | *self-sufficing
test: «One slice of cake will suffice for each child.» What does suffice mean here? | *Be enough | Be shared with the dog | Be bigger | Be wasted
test: Which word is a form of suffice? | suffer | sunny | sudden | *sufficed
exam: Kofi writes «Suffice it to say, the match was cancelled.» What does this phrase tell the reader? | I will say everything I know about the match | The match was a great success | I am angry about the match | *I will only say this, because it is enough
